From cbe93314d5d4fbf36a305ea0ab44281faef63865 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:01:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] Add a batteryless edition of GBA Link Cable Dumper for
 quick save backups

make_batteryless_dumper.py swaps a new GBA side (bldumper.c) into FIX94's
GBA Link Cable Dumper v1.6 boot.dol, keeping the Wii side and its protocol.
On batteryless carts the dumper's backup save and restore save then read
and write the save area in ROM: seconds instead of a full ROM dump. The
save area is found through the cart's batteryless boot code (the entry
point jumps to it), so a restore cut off by a power loss can be redone.
Restores are shown and confirmed on the GBA.

Save writing (savecore.c, shared with the save writer) no longer uses a
test area: only the save area is erased, by commands sent inside it as the
cart's own save routine does, everything is erased before anything is
programmed, and parts left unerased by blocks smaller than CFI reports get
a second pass. A power cut can then always be recovered by writing again.

Tests replay the dumper's Wii side in Python against the emulated GBA:
backup, restore on every board, cancel, invalid files, power cuts, clear,
game and BIOS dumps; and the patcher on a synthetic dol.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
